WEBVTT

00:55.290 --> 00:56.330
<i>Are you watching me?</i>

00:56.810 --> 00:58.950
<i>I've come so far with this body.</i>

00:58.950 --> 01:04.540
<b>Ushio
Family
Grave</b>

00:59.730 --> 01:02.520
<i>I'll win the Inter High.</i>

01:07.710 --> 01:10.710
<b>National
High
School
Sports
Tournament</b>

01:07.710 --> 01:10.710
<b>National
High
School
Sumo
Championship</b>

01:12.820 --> 01:16.590
Good! He's won three individual bouts,
which means he's qualified.

01:17.070 --> 01:19.850
Hinomaru-kun's on top form today.

01:20.520 --> 01:22.850
So Onimaru's back, huh?

01:22.850 --> 01:25.530
He took the "training for three
years ahead" thing to heart, huh?

01:25.530 --> 01:26.850
His patience is impressive.

01:27.440 --> 01:31.890
But he won't beat me while he still
has that look on his face.

01:32.980 --> 01:35.280
All eyes are on me again.

01:35.780 --> 01:39.640
I'll exert myself in sumo today.

01:41.070 --> 01:43.120
<i>On the west side, Hayashi-kun.</i>

01:43.240 --> 01:45.160
<i>On the east side, Tennoji-kun.</i>

01:55.620 --> 01:56.300
Spirit!

02:00.850 --> 02:02.050
The bout is decided!

02:02.050 --> 02:03.330
East side wins!

02:06.360 --> 02:08.810
I'm going to put an end to Hakuro's reign.

02:09.250 --> 02:11.400
Sosuke, do you think you can beat him?

02:12.140 --> 02:14.860
If I didn't, I wouldn't be here.

02:15.990 --> 02:18.610
Tottori Hakuro's Tennoji Shido.

02:18.970 --> 02:21.910
The reigning champ of high school sumo.

02:22.870 --> 02:27.890
Drawing him so early in the individual
tournament was a stroke of bad luck.

02:28.350 --> 02:31.630
If I look unlucky, that suits me just fine.

02:32.430 --> 02:36.730
The whole reason I'm here is to
upset the odds and do the impossible.

02:37.190 --> 02:41.510
I'll beat Tennoji the champion
and show everyone

02:41.770 --> 02:44.530
there's another incredible fighter here!

04:16.480 --> 04:20.990
<b>Bout 15
"Onimaru Kunitsuna
and Dojikiri Yasutsuna"</b>

04:16.570 --> 04:18.730
My impressions of Ushio-kun?

04:18.990 --> 04:20.510
He's strong.

04:20.510 --> 04:25.610
I have nothing but respect for him
for making it here with his physique.

04:25.610 --> 04:30.420
I may not look it now, 
but I used to be quite small myself.

04:30.420 --> 04:32.660
Everyone else in my family
is small of stature,

04:32.660 --> 04:36.500
so I'm truly grateful to the sumo gods
for blessing me with this body.

04:38.780 --> 04:39.620
Okay.

04:39.620 --> 04:40.880
Hinomaru!

04:41.110 --> 04:44.390
I know there's no need to tell you
this since you know it already,

04:44.390 --> 04:45.880
but I'm gonna say it anyway:

04:46.280 --> 04:47.400
Go out there and win!

04:47.400 --> 04:50.010
Go become the high school yokozuna!

04:50.460 --> 04:51.280
Yeah!

04:52.450 --> 04:55.890
<i>Your admission to the
pro league is on the line.</i>

04:56.240 --> 04:59.450
<i>Tennoji-san is someone I really respect.</i>

04:59.870 --> 05:02.860
<i>He was the middle school 
and high school yokozuna.</i>

05:03.380 --> 05:07.320
<i>I get to fight someone who's already
walked down the same path I'm walking.</i>

05:07.580 --> 05:09.490
<i>On the east side, Ushio-kun.</i>

05:09.490 --> 05:11.300
<i>On the west side, Tennoji-kun.</i>

05:12.330 --> 05:15.830
<i>I'll beat him and go on to take the crown!</i>

05:19.270 --> 05:22.310
Their spirits are so intense, you can
feel them up here in the second floor.

05:22.310 --> 05:25.340
When I think about how it must feel
in the ring, I get a chill up my spine.

05:25.800 --> 05:28.750
<i>He is the yokozuna of this space.</i>

05:28.750 --> 05:31.550
<i>A weak-spirited opponent
would be engulfed by his aura</i>

05:31.550 --> 05:35.350
<i>and wouldn't be able to
fight to his full ability.</i>

05:35.670 --> 05:39.080
<i>But that's only true for the weak-spirited.</i>

05:41.340 --> 05:44.610
<i>With the confidence and resolve 
he's built up for this day,</i>

05:45.190 --> 05:47.610
<i>he can even take on a yokozuna.</i>

06:05.380 --> 06:06.220
Spirit!

06:08.220 --> 06:09.800
<i>A f-forearm charge?!</i>

06:12.040 --> 06:15.020
<i>He hit Hinomaru's head despite 
his low stance and speed?!</i>

06:16.390 --> 06:17.480
<i>He's fast.</i>

06:17.480 --> 06:21.230
<i>What's more, he went from that wild
forearm charge to a precise grapple.</i>

06:21.530 --> 06:24.470
<i>The boss built up momentum from the off.</i>

06:24.470 --> 06:27.790
<i>It's the captain's first time
fighting someone so short.</i>

06:27.790 --> 06:29.990
<i>But he didn't hesitate for a moment.</i>

06:32.420 --> 06:35.770
<i>That precise movement he did
to grab his mawashi belt...</i>

06:35.770 --> 06:38.500
<i>He's much more skilled
than his size would suggest.</i>

06:38.900 --> 06:40.670
<i>Tennoji Shido.</i>

06:40.670 --> 06:44.000
<i>He has been blessed with size,
measuring 188 cm now,</i>

06:44.380 --> 06:48.470
<i>but in elementary school,
he wasn't considered large by any means.</i>

06:49.080 --> 06:52.070
<i>You can't bank on having a growth spurt.</i>

06:52.070 --> 06:55.850
<i>Even so, he trained in techniques
that would help him survive.</i>

06:56.340 --> 07:00.300
<i>He's already trodden the 
path that Hinomaru is on.</i>

07:01.530 --> 07:03.970
<i>But now, looking back at
what he went through,</i>

07:03.970 --> 07:07.500
<i>it seems like he was on a path
laid by the sumo gods to make him</i>

07:07.500 --> 07:09.960
<i>the strongest of sumo wrestlers.</i>

07:10.340 --> 07:12.860
<i>It's like they'd said to Tennoji Shido:</i>

07:13.680 --> 07:15.430
<i>"Enter the ring."</i>

07:20.970 --> 07:26.090
<i>What new ordeal will you put
me through now, sumo gods?</i>

07:28.410 --> 07:30.920
<i>Stay out of this!</i>

07:32.100 --> 07:34.500
<i>Onimaru has speed on his side.</i>

07:34.860 --> 07:37.700
<i>Strength, too. But that's not all.</i>

07:37.700 --> 07:40.560
<i>He can shield his own mawashi belt
and seize his opponent's.</i>

07:40.910 --> 07:43.140
<i>He's been the smallest for so long,</i>

07:43.140 --> 07:46.810
<i>he's perfected knocking away his 
opponent's hands and counterattacking.</i>

07:47.440 --> 07:50.280
<i>Just give it up, sumo gods!</i>

07:50.280 --> 07:53.280
<i>You'll never take sumo away from me!</i>

07:53.910 --> 07:55.200
Shorty's got the edge!

07:55.430 --> 07:56.700
No, not yet!

07:59.950 --> 08:04.160
<i>I already know, Ushio-kun, about how
you knock hands aside and counterattack,</i>

08:04.160 --> 08:08.890
<i>and how the main aim of your attack 
is to get a firm grip with your right hand.</i>

08:08.890 --> 08:09.960
<i>Your left doesn't matter.</i>

08:10.290 --> 08:13.970
<i>If I seal off your right hand, 
your offensive power is halved.</i>

08:17.260 --> 08:18.410
Throwing with his left!

08:18.410 --> 08:19.260
He's forcing him over!

08:19.260 --> 08:22.270
<i>You're using a throw to create 
an opening for your right hand.</i>

08:23.750 --> 08:24.520
<i>In that case...</i>

08:25.270 --> 08:27.230
<i>Quick as a flash, you change it up,</i>

08:27.230 --> 08:28.900
<i>and go for throat strikes instead.</i>

08:29.210 --> 08:30.360
<i>There.</i>

08:31.860 --> 08:34.360
<i>I'm prepared for anything you can dish out.</i>

08:36.420 --> 08:38.650
<i>He's not reacting to an incoming move.</i>

08:38.650 --> 08:41.080
<i>He's anticipating what he's about to do.</i>

08:41.080 --> 08:44.000
<i>He's really done his homework on Hinomaru.</i>

08:44.610 --> 08:46.120
<i>Not just on Ushio-kun.</i>

08:46.120 --> 08:47.000
<i>On everyone here.</i>

08:47.490 --> 08:49.090
Kanamori Tsuyoshi.

08:49.380 --> 08:53.550
He's hard to shift once he hankers down,
but he can't react to a fast attack.

08:54.060 --> 08:56.560
You spend all your free
time watching bouts.

08:57.180 --> 08:58.590
It's my hobby.

08:58.590 --> 09:01.060
It's fun to watch all these
different styles of sumo.

09:01.060 --> 09:06.010
And a yokozuna can still lose to
wrestlers who aren't ozeki or yokozuna.

09:07.340 --> 09:09.980
I don't want to let anyone beat me.

09:11.080 --> 09:15.130
<i>He knows how hard it is 
to keep winning in sumo.</i>

09:15.480 --> 09:17.550
<i>That's why he keeps his ego in check</i>

09:17.550 --> 09:20.530
<i>and always prepares
thoroughly for his bouts.</i>

09:20.530 --> 09:23.040
<i>As a result, he's never lost
a bout in high school.</i>

09:25.540 --> 09:29.950
Grabbing someone so much larger
than him must be quite a strain.

09:30.740 --> 09:32.400
This guy's not so tough.

09:33.450 --> 09:35.190
<i>Having a rough time, Ushio-kun?</i>

09:35.190 --> 09:36.930
<i>I bet you are.</i>

09:38.630 --> 09:40.100
<i>You poor thing.</i>

09:40.820 --> 09:43.860
<i>There isn't a sumo wrestler your size
out there who can match you.</i>

09:43.860 --> 09:46.290
<i>But, Ushio-kun, you must've realized...</i>

09:46.960 --> 09:50.580
<i>No other sumo wrestler looks like
he's suffering as much as you do.</i>

09:51.500 --> 09:53.280
<i>Let's get this over with.</i>

09:55.020 --> 09:58.280
<i>It hurts watching you suffer like this!</i>

09:58.730 --> 10:01.280
You don't know the first 
thing about Hinomaru.

10:05.700 --> 10:09.740
You said you loved sumo 
more than anyone else.

10:10.290 --> 10:14.210
But has anyone ever really 
called you out on that?

10:16.350 --> 10:20.680
<i>Preparing for this day has been
difficult, painful, and discouraging.</i>

10:21.120 --> 10:26.810
<i>But... I've never gotten
tired of sumo! Not even once!</i>

10:31.280 --> 10:35.570
<i>I love sumo... even more than you!</i>

10:41.530 --> 10:45.790
<i>Onimaru... your back is glowing.</i>

10:48.180 --> 10:49.460
<i>A double-handed grip!</i>

10:49.790 --> 10:51.960
<i>He's in position for the 
Hundred-Thousand Demon Drop!</i>

10:51.960 --> 10:54.960
You spent too long testing
the waters, Tennoji.

10:55.170 --> 10:59.470
Once Onimaru's in that 
position, it spells trouble.

10:59.470 --> 11:03.350
<i>He needs to get him off-balance 
before executing the technique.</i>

11:03.660 --> 11:07.350
<i>There are an infinite number of ways to 
get to the Hundred-Thousand Demon Drop.</i>

11:09.000 --> 11:11.260
<i>Rock him back and forth, left and right!</i>

11:11.260 --> 11:14.770
<i>Don't stop! Not until he loses his balance!</i>

11:15.070 --> 11:15.360
<b>Two</b>

11:15.070 --> 11:15.360
<b>Handed</b>

11:15.360 --> 11:15.520
<b>Two</b>

11:15.360 --> 11:15.520
<b>Handed</b>

11:15.380 --> 11:17.470
<i>Two-Handed Demon Storm!</i>

11:15.520 --> 11:18.280
<b>Two</b>

11:15.520 --> 11:18.280
<b>Handed</b>

11:15.940 --> 11:16.230
<b>Demon</b>

11:15.940 --> 11:16.230
<b>Storm</b>

11:16.230 --> 11:16.400
<b>Demon</b>

11:16.230 --> 11:16.400
<b>Storm</b>

11:16.400 --> 11:18.280
<b>Demon</b>

11:16.400 --> 11:18.280
<b>Storm</b>

11:23.340 --> 11:24.660
He jerked him to the side!

11:25.060 --> 11:27.220
<i>Yanking him from side to side...</i>

11:27.220 --> 11:29.260
<i>That's what he did in Nagoya.</i>

11:29.260 --> 11:32.170
<i>I doubt there's footage of that out there.</i>

11:32.540 --> 11:36.800
<i>Before, he'd go straight from that stance 
into the Hundred-Thousand Demon Drop.</i>

11:37.100 --> 11:39.830
<i>One-shot techniques are nothing to fear.</i>

11:40.670 --> 11:47.010
<i>But Onimaru's now willing to even use
his hundred-thousand demons as a setup.</i>

11:47.930 --> 11:53.350
<i>Even you will have trouble anticipating
what Onimaru's going to do next.</i>

11:55.230 --> 12:00.280
<i>Maybe running into Tennoji-kun
so early on was a good thing.</i>

12:00.280 --> 12:04.870
<i>He faced him before he'd showed his hand,
and he's close to peak physical condition.</i>

12:05.670 --> 12:09.260
<i>He caught me unaware several 
times in the training hall.</i>

12:09.260 --> 12:12.540
<i>Once he's in that stance,
even a pro would find it hard to escape.</i>

12:14.040 --> 12:14.980
His mawashi belt!

12:14.980 --> 12:16.040
He brute-forced a grip!

12:17.560 --> 12:19.050
He's still flinging him around!

12:19.320 --> 12:20.310
<i>Go!</i>

12:20.310 --> 12:22.550
<i>His arm strength isn't 
enough to stop your twists!</i>

12:22.770 --> 12:26.510
<i>Create a bigger whirlpool 
and suck Tennoji in!</i>

12:26.790 --> 12:27.510
He's off-balance!

12:27.510 --> 12:28.510
Finish him!

12:32.310 --> 12:32.560
<b>Hundred
Demon
Take
Down</b>

12:32.400 --> 12:33.950
<i>Hundred Demon Takedown!</i>

12:32.560 --> 12:32.770
<b>Hundred
Demon
Take
Down</b>

12:32.770 --> 12:35.520
<b>Hundred
Demon
Take
Down</b>

12:36.520 --> 12:37.560
That's...

12:37.560 --> 12:38.770
Hinomaru-san's technique!

12:45.700 --> 12:45.950
<b>Hundred
Demon
Take
Down</b>

12:45.840 --> 12:47.660
<i>Hundred Demon Takedown!</i>

12:45.950 --> 12:46.160
<b>Hundred
Demon
Take
Down</b>

12:46.160 --> 12:47.660
<b>Hundred
Demon
Take
Down</b>

12:48.570 --> 12:51.940
He's taller than Onimaru,
so it looks a little different...

12:51.940 --> 12:54.670
But it also looks ten times stronger!

12:55.240 --> 12:58.700
<i>He was biding his time,
waiting for an opening to strike.</i>

12:58.700 --> 13:01.170
<i>A throw to counter a throw...
That's the mark of a champion!</i>

13:01.370 --> 13:04.170
<i>So this is your new style of sumo?</i>

13:04.700 --> 13:07.400
<i>Those three years of middle 
school you spent in a rut</i>

13:07.400 --> 13:10.350
<i>gave you more than just pain, it seems.</i>

13:10.940 --> 13:15.940
<i>I have much to learn about sumo and the fire
that burns inside those who practice it!</i>

13:20.460 --> 13:21.360
Not yet.

13:21.960 --> 13:23.310
He won't lay down and die yet!

13:25.000 --> 13:28.010
<i>You sure are strong, Tennoji-san.</i>

13:28.550 --> 13:30.980
<i>I've always respected your strength.</i>

13:31.720 --> 13:35.420
<i>The first time I saw you fight
is forever etched on my mind.</i>

13:36.380 --> 13:39.730
<i>Even though you were small, you were strong.</i>

13:40.600 --> 13:43.160
<i>I watched the video of 
your bout so many times,</i>

13:43.510 --> 13:45.050
<i>I started dreaming about it.</i>

13:45.990 --> 13:48.280
<i>Everyone around me got bigger.</i>

13:48.280 --> 13:53.060
<i>Even if I wasn't winning, just watching
you that day made me feel stronger.</i>

13:53.760 --> 13:55.810
<i>You showed me even small guys can win.</i>

13:57.140 --> 13:58.420
<i>I'm grateful for that.</i>

13:58.970 --> 14:03.400
<i>You may have gotten bigger,
but you're still my yardstick!</i>

14:04.270 --> 14:06.780
<i>You're always there at
the top, shining brightly!</i>

14:13.330 --> 14:14.910
<i>So strong...</i>

14:15.170 --> 14:18.470
<i>Which makes me want
to beat you all the more!</i>

14:18.470 --> 14:19.600
<i>He's picked his moment!</i>

14:19.600 --> 14:20.670
<i>He's pushing.</i>

14:20.970 --> 14:25.920
<i>He made Tennoji focus on avoiding a throw
and then took advantage of it...</i>

14:26.080 --> 14:31.760
<i>This is my last technique to unbalance you,
after all the time I've spent admiring you!</i>

14:32.680 --> 14:34.010
<i>The push was a bluff.</i>

14:34.390 --> 14:37.520
<i>Tennoji's weight moved
forward to resist the push.</i>

14:37.700 --> 14:39.270
<i>He can land it now!</i>

14:39.520 --> 14:40.270
<i>Go...</i>

14:40.430 --> 14:42.010
Go!

14:47.150 --> 14:48.150
What?!

14:50.030 --> 14:51.530
He outmaneuvered him?!

14:51.710 --> 14:53.530
<i>How could he evade it?</i>

14:53.930 --> 14:56.660
<i>He wasn't resisting the 
push with all his strength.</i>

14:56.660 --> 14:59.750
<i>He kept some in reserve
to counter the next move.</i>

15:00.110 --> 15:02.610
<i>Ushio-kun's attack was perfect.</i>

15:02.610 --> 15:06.260
<i>But my brother's love 
of sumo is just too great.</i>

15:06.820 --> 15:11.950
<i>He grabs all the info he can find on
wrestlers he's likely to face and studies it.</i>

15:11.950 --> 15:13.930
<i>But that's not all he does.</i>

15:14.360 --> 15:21.030
<i>He envisions how they might develop
and all the ways he could lose to them.</i>

15:21.950 --> 15:25.160
<i>Rocking side to side, exchanging throws,
then a push followed by his triple combo</i>

15:25.160 --> 15:28.200
<i>would certainly be a path
to victory for Ushio-kun.</i>

15:28.200 --> 15:29.000
<i>But...</i>

15:29.330 --> 15:33.990
<i>My brother had already come up
with a plan to counter it!</i>

15:34.340 --> 15:35.990
<i>He's a fearsome opponent.</i>

15:36.810 --> 15:39.050
<i>When I imagine my opponents,</i>

15:39.050 --> 15:42.550
<i>they're usually bigger than the real deal.</i>

15:42.550 --> 15:47.160
<i>The worst-case scenarios I build my strategy
around are nearly always unfounded.</i>

15:47.160 --> 15:48.260
<i>But...</i>

15:48.830 --> 15:50.600
<i>Not with you.</i>

15:50.960 --> 15:52.520
<i>Your blade...</i>

15:53.880 --> 15:56.500
<i>was indeed pressed against
the base of my throat.</i>

15:57.520 --> 15:59.640
<i>I used to be small, too...</i>

16:00.050 --> 16:02.480
<i>Right up until my first year
of middle school.</i>

16:03.560 --> 16:06.610
<i>I barely avoided having to wander
through that merciless hell.</i>

16:06.610 --> 16:10.750
<i>But you've walked through it and come out
the other side to stand here now...</i>

16:11.060 --> 16:13.160
<i>You're incredible!</i>

16:14.530 --> 16:17.530
<i>But you're too tense,
and it shows on your face.</i>

16:18.470 --> 16:20.790
<i>You want to be a yokozuna, right?</i>

16:20.790 --> 16:23.140
<i>A yokozuna is the best of the best!</i>

16:23.140 --> 16:27.000
<i>If that's your goal, try to
enjoy the bouts a little more!</i>

16:28.090 --> 16:29.550
<i>You love sumo, right?</i>

16:30.050 --> 16:31.550
<i>You enjoy it, right?</i>

16:31.550 --> 16:35.190
<i>Then, no matter what setbacks you face,</i>

16:35.870 --> 16:37.350
<i>you hafta smile!</i>

16:36.100 --> 16:36.430
<b>Six
Point
Torso
Slice</b>

16:36.430 --> 16:36.800
<b>Six
Point
Torso
Slice</b>

16:36.800 --> 16:39.060
<b>Six
Point
Torso
Slice</b>

16:37.350 --> 16:39.060
<i>Six Point Torso Slice!</i>

16:52.140 --> 16:54.320
<i>What's with that look in his eye?</i>

16:54.650 --> 16:56.910
<i>One last desperate act?</i>

16:59.290 --> 17:02.160
<i>Still, that's exactly...</i>

17:06.470 --> 17:08.670
<i>...what makes you so darn cool!</i>

17:27.270 --> 17:28.810
West side wins.

17:28.810 --> 17:31.900
<i>Tennoji-kun wins with an arm-lock throw.</i>

17:44.960 --> 17:47.790
<i>You've given me plenty 
to think about, Onimaru.</i>

17:47.790 --> 17:49.590
<i>I won't celebrate my victory,</i>

17:50.660 --> 17:55.140
<i>not out of gratitude for showing me that,
but out of respect for your style.</i>

17:58.080 --> 18:00.510
<i>Since he doesn't meet
the height requirements,</i>

18:00.510 --> 18:05.670
<i>his only path to the pro league was to become
the high school yokozuna at the Inter High</i>

18:06.080 --> 18:10.520
<i>and enter the All-Japan 
National Championships.</i>

18:11.110 --> 18:12.400
<i>And now, that path...</i>

18:13.100 --> 18:14.090
<i>has closed.</i>

18:17.740 --> 18:19.660
Oh damn, I lost!

18:19.660 --> 18:21.740
He's really strong, isn't he?

18:22.850 --> 18:24.930
But no use crying over spilled milk.

18:24.930 --> 18:26.750
The team tournament's up next.

18:26.960 --> 18:28.710
I need to just shake it off.

18:28.710 --> 18:30.750
I'm still a first-year, after all.

18:31.500 --> 18:33.750
I'll get my chance to join 
the pro league next year.

18:34.040 --> 18:37.990
<i>No, Tennoji won't be here next year.</i>

18:37.990 --> 18:41.550
<i>And you worked so hard to beat him...</i>

18:41.840 --> 18:44.660
So what order are we going in
for the team tournament?

18:44.660 --> 18:45.310
Where's Kirihito?

18:45.620 --> 18:47.770
You don't need to fight
in the team tournament.

18:51.150 --> 18:52.020
Captain...

18:52.020 --> 18:53.070
But...

18:53.700 --> 18:54.750
Why not?

18:54.750 --> 18:57.130
We talked it over and made a decision.

18:59.720 --> 19:01.110
You're hurt, aren't you?

19:01.110 --> 19:03.370
We're not falling for it again!

19:04.480 --> 19:06.590
I'm fine! This is nothing.

19:06.590 --> 19:09.060
Tsuji's calling a taxi right now.

19:09.060 --> 19:10.460
You're going to the hospital.

19:11.320 --> 19:13.120
What about our promise?!

19:13.120 --> 19:15.090
We're going to make Dachi High
the best in Japan!

19:15.340 --> 19:16.210
Hey!

19:17.140 --> 19:18.960
The individual tournament...

19:18.960 --> 19:24.230
Getting into the pro league was my
mountain to climb! But Dachi High winning...

19:24.720 --> 19:26.930
We all dreamed of making that happen!

19:27.390 --> 19:33.100
This is the only year you and Yuma
will be on the Dachi High team...

19:33.930 --> 19:35.440
So please!

19:36.540 --> 19:39.720
I want to make at least one dream come true!

19:43.460 --> 19:44.610
I'm sorry.

19:46.120 --> 19:48.030
It's okay. Just rest up for today.

19:48.030 --> 19:50.750
Get ready for the bouts 
tomorrow and the day after.

19:51.880 --> 19:54.250
You're not done yet, Ushio.

19:54.640 --> 19:59.760
Your dream of joining the pro league 
may come true in the team tournament.

20:01.930 --> 20:05.700
But I thought Shorty had to win to
become the high school yokozuna

20:05.700 --> 20:08.090
and enter the All-Japan 
National Championships.

20:08.090 --> 20:10.460
That's how it usually works, yeah.

20:10.460 --> 20:13.000
But more than one wrestler
can attain that mantle.

20:13.000 --> 20:14.000
What?!

20:15.120 --> 20:17.980
For the past two years,
Tennoji has been so rampant,

20:17.980 --> 20:20.260
he was the only one given the honor.

20:20.260 --> 20:24.080
But in previous years, there were two,
sometimes even three who were given it.

20:24.370 --> 20:29.870
Okay, but since he's still running rampant,
surely he'll be the only one chosen again?

20:30.080 --> 20:33.650
Yes, Tennoji Shido is all-conquering.

20:33.650 --> 20:38.510
But if someone gave him his first loss,
then even if it was in the team tournament...

20:39.580 --> 20:42.240
There's no guarantee it'll work, though.

20:42.240 --> 20:46.090
His team might lose to some other
team before we draw them.

20:46.090 --> 20:49.850
Th-Then, we'll just beat 
whichever team beats Tennoji!

20:50.870 --> 20:52.850
That's the plan, anyway.

20:53.030 --> 20:58.450
It's not a huge chance, I know,
but we haven't exhausted all avenues yet.

20:59.870 --> 21:04.360
The master knows a good doctor, 
so be sure to come back to us after.

21:04.730 --> 21:08.870
While you're doing that, we'll make sure
we survive the team tournament bouts.

21:09.550 --> 21:12.870
You said getting to the pro league
was your mountain to climb,

21:13.310 --> 21:15.950
but now, it's our dream, too.

21:15.950 --> 21:20.410
We'll give you another chance to become
the strongest high school sumo wrestler!

21:20.410 --> 21:23.050
Yeah, don't carry it all on your shoulders.

21:23.050 --> 21:25.200
You can count on us, Hinomaru-san!

21:25.200 --> 21:26.510
It'll be a cakewalk.

21:26.860 --> 21:28.810
Let's do it, Ushio.

21:28.810 --> 21:31.140
We'll win and win again,
and keep on winning!

21:31.140 --> 21:36.020
Let's make those big shots 
beg you to come to Nationals!

21:39.670 --> 21:40.650
Yeah...

23:16.000 --> 23:19.750
<b>Shopping date with Yuma</b>

23:16.450 --> 23:19.970
The Odachi High School 
sumo club's Gojo Yuma.

23:19.970 --> 23:23.770
His henchmen are
Hashi, Funaki and Saigo.

23:20.160 --> 23:23.500
<b>Hashi, Funaki and Saigo came, too</b>

23:23.770 --> 23:26.610
Dachi High's mascot is Chanko.

23:23.920 --> 23:26.510
<b>Yuma giving Chanko a snack
So cute</b>

23:26.610 --> 23:27.840
So cute.

23:27.510 --> 23:31.010
<b>Next Bout  "National Treasure is Delicious"</b>

23:27.840 --> 23:30.310
Uh, Bro... What are you doing?
